"kind":"news","tone":"blue"}],"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1968487/000119312526133381/0001193125-26-133381-index.htm"},{"date":"2026-03-26","form":"8-K","codes":["2.02","8.01","9.01"],"events":[{"label":"Results announced","kind":"results","tone":"blue"},{"label":"Other material event","kind":"news","tone":"blue"}],"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1968487/000196848726000003/0001968487-26-000003-index.htm"}],"legal_events":[{"date":"2023-12-11","label":"Activist or control stake disclosed","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1968487/000119312523292612/0001193125-23-292612-index.htm","tone":"warn"}],"summary":{"sentences":["Worthington Steel, Inc. files with the SEC under \"Steel Works, Blast Furnaces & Rolling & Finishing Mills\", based in OH, and has been publicly reporting for 2 years.","It reported $3.2bn of revenue over the trailing four quarters, up 12.0% against the same quarter a year earlier, at a gross margin of 9.9%.","Listed on NYSE, it funds itself from operations ($232.9m of operating cash flow over the year)."],"generated":true,"note":"Assembled from filing metadata and XBRL figures. Not editorial judgement - and rule 7 asks whether *you* can explain it, so rewrite this in your own words before you rely on it."},"bull":[{"text":"Revenue grew 12.0% year on year (Q1 2026 vs Q1 2025), reaching $769.8m in the quarter.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1968487/000196848726000008/0001968487-26-000008-index.htm","accession":"0001968487-26-000008"},{"text":"Operating cash flow is positive at $232.9m over the trailing year, so the business funds itself and is not dependent on raising money.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1968487/000119312525237107/0001193125-25-237107-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-25-237107"},{"text":"Net cash of $13.2m against total assets of $2.3bn - no debt overhang forcing decisions.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1968487/000196848726000026/0001968487-26-000026-index.htm","accession":"0001968487-26-000026"},{"text":"Share count is close to flat (0.8% over the year), so growth in the business accrues to existing holders rather than being diluted away.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1968487/000196848726000008/0001968487-26-000008-index.htm","accession":"0001968487-26-000008"}],"bear":[{"text":"Gross margin compressed from 11.8% to 9.9% against the same quarter a year earlier. Either input costs are rising or the company is discounting to hold volume.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1968487/000196848726000008/0001968487-26-000008-index.htm","accession":"0001968487-26-000008"},{"text":"Gross margin is only 9.9%, so scale has to be enormous before anything reaches the bottom line.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1968487/000196848726000008/0001968487-26-000008-index.htm","accession":"0001968487-26-000008"},{"text":"Officers and directors hold only 1.6% of the shares. There is little alignment between what happens to the share price and what happens to them.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1968487/000119312526298680/0001193125-26-298680-index.htm"},{"text":"Base rate: 57.8% of US common stocks underperformed one-month Treasury bills over their lifetimes (Bessembinder, Journal of Financial Economics, 2018). Nothing above changes that starting point.","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2018.06.004"}],"triggers":[{"id":"gross_margin_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Gross margin falls below 2.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"gross_margin","comparison":"below","threshold":0.02,"consecutive":2,"current":0.099,"current_display":"9.9%","threshold_display":"2.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Eight points of margin is a real deterioration rather than noise. Two consecutive quarters stops one bad quarter from forcing a sale.","editable":true},{"id":"growth_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Revenue 